## The question that is yours (G7)

§8.3 item 5 makes the efficiency pass a **rung-freeze criterion**, and §16 names the Efficiency
sheet as the ledger it reads. So R0 cannot freeze while that ledger has no emitter — but M0-T5
is a generator change, not census work, and M0 could arguably close without it.

Two options, both defensible, and it is not mine to pick:
1. **M0-T5 lands inside M0.** M0 does not close until the §19 ledger emits. Cleanest against
   §8.3, costs M0 some wall clock.
2. **G7 deferral to before R0's freeze.** M0 closes on the census dimension; the deferral is
   recorded so the cockpit does not read green on an unstarted §19 ledger, and R0's freeze gate
   picks it up.

My recommendation is (2) — the ledger is consumed at *freeze* time, not at census time, and
deferring it keeps M0's exit criteria about the catalogue. But it only works if the deferral is
recorded, because an unrecorded "later" is exactly the H4 pattern PARĪKṢAKA just caught.

— SŪTRADHĀRA
